1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,640
The Marriage of Figaro, episode ten: the letter with the pin.

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:10,720
The Countess, alone, remembers: Dove sono, where are the beautiful moments of sweetness and love? She will win her husband back.

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:19,380
She dictates, Susanna writes, Sull'aria: what a gentle breeze tonight, under the pines. The letter is sealed with a pin; the Count must send the pin back as his answer.

4
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:26,830
Village girls bring flowers to the Countess. Among them a shy one: Cherubino in a dress. Antonio pulls off the bonnet. Caught again!

5
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:36,620
The Count wants to punish him, but Barbarina speaks up: you kissed me, sir, and promised me whatever I want. I want Cherubino as my husband. The Count is trapped by his own promises.

6
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:46,220
The double wedding begins with a fandango. Kneeling for her bridal wreath, Susanna slips the Count the letter. He pricks his finger on the pin, drops it, then picks it up and pins it to his sleeve.

7
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:51,760
Figaro sees and laughs: some girl has sent the Count a love note. He has no idea it was his bride.

8
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:54,200
Next episode: Figaro's jealousy.
